This PR enhances the auto-initialization security by adding proper domain verification to ensure the tracker only auto-initializes when loaded from the official `pixel.data.platformance.io` domain.

## Problem
The previous auto-initialization logic only checked if the script `src` contained `tracker.js` but didn't validate the domain. This could potentially allow unauthorized auto-initialization if someone included the tracker from a different domain with the `data-siteid` attribute.

## Solution
Enhanced the auto-initialization logic with robust domain verification:

```javascript
// Before: Only checked for tracker.js filename
if (script.src && script.src.indexOf('tracker.js') !== -1) {
    currentScript = script;
    break;
}

// After: Proper hostname verification with security protections
if (script.src && script.src.indexOf('tracker.js') !== -1) {
    try {
        var tempAnchor = document.createElement('a');
        tempAnchor.href = script.src;
        var hostname = tempAnchor.hostname;

        if (hostname === 'pixel.data.platformance.io') {
            currentScript = script;
            break;
        }
    } catch (e) {
        continue;
    }
}
```

## Security Benefits
- **Domain validation**: Auto-initialization only occurs when script is loaded from `pixel.data.platformance.io`
- **Subdomain spoofing protection**: Prevents attacks using domains like `pixel.data.platformance.io.evil.com`
- **Error handling**: Gracefully handles malformed URLs and edge cases
- **Backward compatibility**: Manual initialization continues to work normally

## Testing
- ✅ Verified auto-initialization fails with non-official domains (expected behavior)
- ✅ Confirmed manual initialization works properly
- ✅ Tested against subdomain spoofing attempts
- ✅ Validated edge cases (empty/null URLs, malformed URLs)

This change ensures that the auto-initialization feature described in the README with `<script data-siteid="YOUR_SITE_ID" src="https://pixel.data.platformance.io/tracker.js"></script>` works securely and only with the official domain.

Fixes #6.

